CLAUDE.md

# E7 conditioning raw arrays: 3.1 MB of dense correlation matrices, regenerable by
# re-running `python -m experiments.e7_interface_ablation --force` (~7 min). The scientific
# content (condition number, singular values, height-distance correlation block, interface
# spread stats) is committed in interface_ablation_conditioning.json. Excluded to respect
# the repo-wide 1000 KB large-file policy (.pre-commit-config.yaml check-added-large-files).
experiments/results/interface_ablation_conditioning.npz

# DATA-01b: the three large E2 artifacts now ship inside the published Zenodo
# real-rig archive under reference_outputs/ (record 21889922), so they left git
# once that archive was public. Ignored here so a local E2 re-run cannot
# re-commit them and re-break the repo-wide 1000 KB large-file guard.
# Regenerate locally with:
#   python -m experiments.e2_real_rig --out experiments/results --force
# reconstruction_errors.csv and reprojection_residuals.csv in the archive are
# byte-identical to the copies removed. calibration.json is NOT: the archive
# ships the 2026-08-10 image-source run, while the copy removed here was the
# 2026-07-31 video-source run. They are the same library (1.8.0) and agree to
# ~1.5e-8 on water_z, but if you need those exact bytes, take them from git
# history at 25655f7, not from the archive.
experiments/results/calibration.json
experiments/results/reprojection_residuals.csv
experiments/results/reconstruction_errors.csv

# E1's per-point spatial-error CSV (experiments/e1_refractive_comparison.py) is
# ~11MB -- 8 depths x 2 models x every adjacent-corner-pair in a dense N_GRID=7
# sweep -- which exceeds this repo's check-added-large-files --maxkb=1000 gate.
# It has no committed baseline (D-20) and is not compared by --check; it is
# fully deterministic and reproduced on demand via
# `python -m experiments.e1_refractive_comparison --out experiments/results --force`.
experiments/results/exp2_spatial_errors.csv

# Seed-sweep working directories. These are noise-floor MEASUREMENTS used to
# decide whether a movement is real (D-19.3-17), not manuscript artifacts: each
# run writes a full experiment output tree per seed, which is large and is
# summarised into MANUSCRIPT-FINDINGS.md rather than committed.
seed_sweep_19_2/
seed_sweep_19_3/

# Dry-run state from experiments/rerun_19_5.sh -- control-flow rehearsal
# only, never a record of a real run (see that script's STATE_FILE block).
experiments/rerun_19_5_state.dryrun.tsv

# Dry-run state from experiments/run_experiment_suite.sh (D-25's stem). The
# path carries the frozen short sha (D-23 as halved by D-48), hence the glob.
# Control-flow rehearsal only, never a record of a real run -- and the whole
# reason it has its own path is that a dry-run state file left where the real
# one lives makes the NEXT real launch a silent no-op (every stage skipped,
# exit 0, no artifacts).
experiments/run_experiment_suite_state.*.dryrun.tsv

# Pre-launch gate log (phase 19.5) -- rerunnable, not an artifact
experiments/prelaunch_gate_19_5.log

# The production queue log IS a citable artifact -- it is the human-readable
# record of which seeds were requested (see the 19.4 band-sidecar todo, which
# cites rerun_19_4.log for exactly that). Un-ignore it against *.log above so
# plan 10 commits it without needing "git add -f".
!experiments/rerun_19_5.log

# Same reasoning for the one driver's own log (D-25's stem): the production
# queue log IS a citable artifact -- the human-readable record of which seeds
# were requested and which stages ran. Un-ignored against *.log above so it is
# committable without "git add -f".
!experiments/run_experiment_suite.log

# E2's band working tree (experiments/results_e2_band, plan 19.5-10, COV-07).
# run_stage_e2_band does `rm -rf` on this directory before every run, so it is
# a working tree, not an artifact store -- committing it whole would rewrite
# 133 files into history on every future band run. It is also ~26 MB of which
# roughly half is byte-identical duplication: seed_N/calibration.json and
# seed_N_e2_out/calibration.json matched by md5 on all three seeds.
#
# What IS citable is 21 KB of it: the three per-seed metric records that
# gate_e2_band reads and that proved seed 42 reproduces the committed
# experiments/results/real_rig_metrics.json within rtol=1e-6, the scope
# declaration, and the three seed configs. Those are un-ignored below; the
# derived bulk (full calibration dumps, reprojection residuals, spatial
# measurements, 87 diagnostic PNGs) is not.
experiments/results_e2_band/*
!experiments/results_e2_band/config_seed*.yaml
!experiments/results_e2_band/e2_band_scope.json
!experiments/results_e2_band/seed_*_e2_out/
experiments/results_e2_band/seed_*_e2_out/*
!experiments/results_e2_band/seed_*_e2_out/real_rig_metrics.json

# E4's repeat stdout (plan 19.5-10, COV-06). Un-ignored against *.log for the
# same reason as rerun_19_5.log above: it is the ONLY surviving record of
# repeat 1's per-stage numbers. Each cell's benchmark.json is overwritten by
# repeat 2 ("Overwriting existing internals artifact ... may be stale from a
# previous config"), so the on-disk records hold repeat 2 only. The ~1.85x
# first-run-slower result rests on repeat 1, and without this log its nfev,
# cost and optimality survive nowhere outside the summary row in
# benchmark_grid_repeat.csv.
!experiments/results_e4_repeat/repeat_stdout.log

# Dataset download cache (download.py writes to <cwd>/aquacal_data, so it lands
# wherever the user runs from -- currently 354 MB under docs/tutorials/). The only
# prior guard was a nested aquacal_data/.gitignore containing "*", which ignores
# itself, is therefore untracked, and does not survive a clone. A bare pattern
# matches at any depth and covers docs/tutorials/aquacal_data/ too.
aquacal_data/

# Second-machine re-run of E4 and E2 on 32 GB Linux (experiments/
# results_linux32gb, see its linux32gb_scope.json). Same DATA-01b policy as
# experiments/results/ above: the three bulk E2 artifacts ship in the Zenodo
# archive under reference_outputs/, not in git, and two of them (2021 KB and
# 1184 KB) would trip check-added-large-files --maxkb=1000. Listed here so a
# future E2 re-run pointed at this directory cannot re-commit them.
experiments/results_linux32gb/e2_*/calibration.json
experiments/results_linux32gb/e2_*/reprojection_residuals.csv
experiments/results_linux32gb/e2_*/reconstruction_errors.csv

# Un-ignored against *.log for the same reason as rerun_19_5.log and
# results_e4_repeat/repeat_stdout.log above -- these are citable records, not
# rerunnable noise. e4/run.log holds the per-cell ELAPSED wall clock, which
# survives nowhere else (benchmark_grid.csv carries per-stage seconds only).
# The e2 logs hold the stage timing table plus the frame accounting (262 usable
# -> 210/52 split -> 200 optimised) that is DATA-01a's gate-1 evidence.
!experiments/results_linux32gb/e4/run.log
!experiments/results_linux32gb/e2_timing/run.log
!experiments/results_linux32gb/e2_memory/run.log
!experiments/results_linux32gb/e2_cv413/run.log

# Phase 23's in-phase verification output directory (D-12). Every run this
# phase's plans schedule lands here at one seed and is never committed; the
# evidence it produces is transcribed into each plan's own 23-0N-SUMMARY.md
# instead.
experiments/verify_23/
experiments/verify_23_optblocks/
experiments/verify_23_fdnoise/

# D-19 / plan 25-05: the Huber-knee probe raw calibration outputs. 13 MB EACH,
# dominated by a 13 MB exp2_spatial_errors.csv per arm -- too large to commit, and
# regenerable from probe_fscale.py at 054d753 (~10 min wall clock for both arms).
# The evidence MF-21 cites is committed and unaffected: FINDINGS.md carries every
# number, fscale_accuracy_comparison.csv carries the derived control-vs-treatment
# comparison, and calls_{control,treatment}.json carry the per-solve records.
# Same policy as experiments/verify_23*/ above: raw run output stays out, the
# transcribed evidence stays in.
.planning/probes/2026-08-17-huber-knee/e1_control/
.planning/probes/2026-08-17-huber-knee/e1_treatment/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 26 / DRIVER-04 (D-28..D-32): the pre-re-run archive.
#
# Every pre-existing output tree moved to experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/ in
# plan 26-01, immediately after the `pre-rerun-baseline` tag. NOTHING was
# deleted -- the archive stays reachable for the whole v2.1 suite re-run
# because E2's ~1e-8 control and E3's tier diff compare against it (D-12), and
# `--baseline-dir` resolves here.
#
# Every literal-prefix rule above that names a moved tree is MIRRORED under the
# new prefix. Without these, the ~128 untracked/ignored files that move with
# those trees would become newly visible in `git status` and newly committable
# -- which would re-break the repo-wide 1000 KB large-file guard the DATA-01b
# rules exist to hold.
#
# The ORIGINAL rules above are deliberately kept: experiments/results/ is where
# the fresh run writes, and the DATA-01b lines must keep applying to it.
#
# Phase 30 / POST-03 purges the archive; this whole block goes with it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Mirrors experiments/results/ (E7 conditioning arrays, DATA-01b E2 bulk, E1 spatial CSV)
experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/results/interface_ablation_conditioning.npz
experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/results/calibration.json
experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/results/reprojection_residuals.csv
experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/results/reconstruction_errors.csv
experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/results/exp2_spatial_errors.csv

# Mirrors experiments/results_e2_band/ (the ~126-file derived bulk stays out)
experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/results_e2_band/*
!experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/results_e2_band/config_seed*.yaml
!experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/results_e2_band/e2_band_scope.json
!experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/results_e2_band/seed_*_e2_out/
experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/results_e2_band/seed_*_e2_out/*
!experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/results_e2_band/seed_*_e2_out/real_rig_metrics.json

# Mirrors experiments/results_linux32gb/ (DATA-01b bulk out, citable run logs in)
experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/results_linux32gb/e2_*/calibration.json
experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/results_linux32gb/e2_*/reprojection_residuals.csv
experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/results_linux32gb/e2_*/reconstruction_errors.csv
!experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/results_linux32gb/e4/run.log
!experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/results_linux32gb/e2_timing/run.log
!experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/results_linux32gb/e2_memory/run.log
!experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/results_linux32gb/e2_cv413/run.log

# Mirrors experiments/results_e4_repeat/repeat_stdout.log
!experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/results_e4_repeat/repeat_stdout.log

# The archived production queue logs stay tracked against *.log (line 59), for
# the same reason the originals were un-ignored: they are the only surviving
# per-stage record of the 19.4 and 19.5 queues.
!experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/driver_state/rerun_19_4.log
!experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/driver_state/rerun_19_5.log

# Mirrors experiments/verify_23*/ -- D-31's untracked probe trees, moved aside
# as LOCAL HYGIENE only (they are gitignored and never travel to the run box).
experiments/pre_rerun_baseline/verify_probes/

# The reduced-scale (--smoke) output trees, written ONLY by
# `bash experiments/run_experiment_suite.sh --smoke`. They are ACCEPTANCE
# EVIDENCE that each stage's invocation line is correct -- never an artifact,
# never a number, and never comparable to anything under experiments/results/.
# The driver forces these directories precisely so a reduced-scale pass cannot
# be mistaken for, or overwrite, a production result (research SP-7).
#
# The glob is deliberate: --smoke re-points every sibling tree too
# (results_smoke_e2_band, _e2_timing, _e2_memory, _e2_invocations,
# _e4_repeat), because run_stage_e2_band's first act is
# `rm -rf "${OUT_DIR_E2_BAND}"` and a rehearsal must not be able to delete the
# production band tree.
experiments/results_smoke/
experiments/results_smoke_*/
